Chapter: BvtScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  subjects-doc : List Text =
    ["A FILE of chapter paths, one per line, which REPLACES the BVT list for",
     "the gate's cited-test run phase. It is this runner rather than a new loop",
     "because the grading lives here: the .expected filter, the .disk sidecar,",
     "and the strict-prefix arithmetic that separates a TRUNCATED capture from",
     "a real mismatch (L-SHORT). test-run.ps1 never sees an .expected and",
     "renders no verdict, so a second loop would be a third verdict site",
     "missing all of it.",
     "A FILE and not a [string[]]: pwsh -File splits an array into separate",
     "positional arguments, so only the first element ever bound and the rest",
     "came back as \"a positional parameter cannot be found\"."]

  bvt-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-default "CodexCdx" SptString (SeLit ""), sh-param-default "Jobs" SptInt (SeInt 8), sh-doc subjects-doc (sh-param-default "SubjectsFile" SptString (SeLit ""))]

Section: S01 -- Preamble

  s01 : List ShellCmd =
    let no-kernel = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"ERROR: No kernel at $stage0 -- run build/build.ps1 first.\"") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in let no-vm = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"ERROR: codex-vm.exe not found at $vmExe\"") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScRaw "Set-Location (Join-Path $PSScriptRoot '..')", ScRaw "[Environment]::CurrentDirectory = (Get-Location).Path"]

Section: S02 -- Test List

 Each entry carries what the test GUARDS. That is the only record of why
 most of them exist, and several say what breaks when the test is weakened,
 so it is a note about defects the fixed point cannot see rather than prose
 about our own code. The list emits one entry per line to keep it readable
 and reviewable in the script it produces.

  bvt-entry : Text, Text -> ShellCmd
  bvt-entry (path) (note) =
    if note == "" then ScRaw ("    '" & path & "'")
    else ScRaw ("    '" & path & "'  # " & note)

  bvt-head : Text -> ShellCmd
  bvt-head (note) = if note == "" then ScRaw "" else ScRaw ("    # " & note)

  bvt-test-list : List ShellCmd = [
    bvt-head "--- Language features the compiler does NOT use ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\typeclass-smoke.codex" "type classes (Show, Eq, Ord)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\typeclass-poly.codex" "a class with a SUPERCLASS: the instance dict must carry __super-<Super>, which was a null pointer in every instance until the desugarer populated it",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\handler-smoke.codex" "effect handlers",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\handler-dotted-discharge.codex" "a family handler (with Store) discharges its dotted members (Store.Read, Store.Write) via the sub-effect lattice; probe declares NO row, so a discharge failure surfaces as CDX2031/CDX2033, not a wrong answer",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\cap-gpu-family.codex" "a bare [Gpu] row is a FAMILY grant and must survive the manifest: it compiled clean and was then DENIED at the window guard (write: -1) because manifest-cap-id did not know the name \"Gpu\". Pins the row -> manifest -> process-cap-word path end to end",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\network-effect.codex" "the Network effect has an IMPLEMENTATION. fetch/post/resolve-dns were effect operations nothing implemented: a call type-checked clean and died at the end of emit with CDX2040, and no test called one so the battery could not see it. This runs headless (resolve-dns on a dotted quad never touches the wire) and still has to LINK, so a removed implementation stops it compiling. It also pins the https refusal TEXT, which is a diagnostic and therefore a feature: the old one said \"TLS is not implemented here\" thirty lines above a working TLS 1.3 handshake in the same chapter",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\linear-smoke.codex" "linear types (consume, freeze)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\mutable-smoke.codex" "mutable records, field mutation",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\try-smoke.codex" "try/retry/fallback",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\with-timeout-test.codex" "timeout construct",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\fork-nested.codex" "concurrency (fork/await)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\unit-smoke.codex" "unit type",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- Library correctness (not exercised by self-compile) ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\hamt-test.codex" "HAMT -- backs Set and KvStore",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\sort-test.codex" "sort with custom comparators",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\crypto-test.codex" "AES, ChaCha20",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- The authentication the release advertises ---",
    bvt-head "None of this is reachable from the compiler, so the fixed point cannot",
    bvt-head "see any of it. Until these landed here the whole claim -- TLS 1.3 with",
    bvt-head "X.509 authentication, two curves, two digests, a real chain verified to",
    bvt-head "its root -- rested on tests run BY HAND, once, by whoever wrote them.",
    bvt-head "Every one of these is a signature check, and a signature check that",
    bvt-head "wrongly answers True is the one bug in the tree with no blast radius",
    bvt-head "short of the whole trust story.",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ecdsa-p256.codex" "P-256 against published vectors",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ecdsa-p384.codex" "P-384 curve arithmetic, the second curve",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ecdsa-sha384.codex" "the CURVE and the DIGEST are independent choices. This asserts a signature must VERIFY, and requires the wrong-digest entry point to FAIL -- without that second half the file passes unchanged if both entry points quietly hash SHA-256, which is how the FIPS 186-4 defect it found (z is the leftmost min(N,outlen) bits, not the digest reduced mod n) stayed invisible",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\x509-parse.codex" "the certificate parser, including the key-algorithm arms whose catch-all silently absorbed KeyEcdsaP384 and stopped every P-384 certificate parsing three stages downstream",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ecdsa-cert.codex" "the REAL github.com chain, verified through its P-384 root. A fixture chain proves the arithmetic; a chain somebody else issued proves the parser agrees with the world",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\real-cert.codex" "RFC 6125 hostname matching, with no commonName fallback",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\tls-cv-schemes.codex" "CertificateVerify under every scheme the ClientHello offers, signed by OpenSSL and checked here. Also the only thing making the offered set and the accepted set agree: they are written in two places and nothing else compares them",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\tls-test.codex" "the ClientHello we SEND, decoded back and pinned by SIZE (len 169, size 174). Everything above checks what we ACCEPT; nothing checked what we OFFER, and the offered set has no other reader. Adding one signature scheme to tls-ext-sig-algs is one extra uint16, so the P-384 scheme point at main 11688 moved both numbers and left this red on main while the gate that shipped it stayed green. Also the only BVT coverage of x25519 and of the record layer",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\dtls-hello.codex" "the same size pins on the other transport (ch1 146, ch2 160, and ch2 must be the LONGER -- the second hello echoes the server's cookie), moved by the same 2 bytes and red for the same reason. The assertion that earns its keep is dtls-is-hrr: in DTLS 1.3 a HelloRetryRequest is not a message type, it is a ServerHello carrying a magic random, so a receiver that switches on message type never sees one and the cookie exchange -- the whole DoS defence -- silently never engages. It also requires an extension list truncated past its own length to be REFUSED rather than read, because garbage read there becomes a shared secret",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\web-chain.codex" "the seven shipped trust anchors, and a live www.digicert.com chain walked to one of them with the hostname checked. Runs offline -- the chain is embedded. It asserts supplied, parsed AND can-verify separately, because a root that parses is not a root that can be used: both P-384 roots parsed cleanly for the whole time they were deliberately excluded, typing KeyEcdsaOther with x509-can-verify False. Sabotaging that predicate moves the can-verify line alone and leaves supplied/parsed at 7",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- Codegen stress (caught regressions the fixed point misses) ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\lir-selector-smoke.codex" "the LIR selector's correctness shapes, one boot: a shadowed-global call that must go indirect not direct (answered -1 for 7), a join-into-join coalesce that must refuse or the structural verifier halts a valid program (CDX9007), a compound-accumulator tail call the tree emitter miscompiles and the selector gets right (9 for 8), the 5-param col-hue parallel-move clash (red as yellow), and the result-is-a-use coalesce (RAX garbage for the result). Every one is a wrong ANSWER the fixed point cannot see; pinned by .expected",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\noise-test.codex" "arithmetic-heavy pure leaves (Noise/Perlin gradient math); caught the Tier 2 non-TCO leaf temp-pool miscompile (CL 6387 widening)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\tco-nested-if.codex" "TCO if-chain with a nested-if arm body; guards the jmp-end elision miscompile that silently skipped the arm (CL 6430)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\tco-shuffle-spill.codex" "the tree emitter's tail-call shuffle with a SPILLED parameter. Repro of the miscompile fixed at main 10065; the program hung forever and the fixed point, all nine benches and the BVT stayed green through it. The shuffle planner has no verifier and roughly three quarters of every compile is emitted by it, so these two repros are the only thing standing under it",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\tco-direct-arg-reads.codex" "the same planner, the other bug: an argument that reads a parameter the shuffle has already overwritten. Repro of the miscompile fixed at main 10099, which answered 1001 where 101 is correct, with no diagnostic and no fault",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ops\\real-approx-equality.codex" "`~` and `~0` on an f32. Real has no `==` (CDX2085 refuses it), so these two ARE its equality, and neither took a type: the ordinal transform broadcasts the sign with `sar 63` while an f32's sign sits at bit 31, so every single looked positive. Measured before the fix: f32 `-0 ~ +0` answered False while the identical f64 pair answered True. The f64 lines are the control -- they are what says the defect was about width rather than about the comparison",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ops\\real-mode-opening.codex" "an `opening` that RETURNS a moded Real. emit-opening-result-print matched RealTy alone and its tail emits nothing, so such a program printed NO OUTPUT for as long as the modes existed. real-mode-show cannot see it: `show` inside an act block is a different walk that was always right, so a test that PRINTS a moded Real is not a test that RETURNS one",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ops\\real-mode-fields.codex" "the sibling walk, emit-opening-print-field, whose tail is emit-inline-itoa-and-print -- so a moded Real field printed its BIT PATTERN, a plausible number in the right place. Must be a constructor, not a record: emit-opening-result-print has no RecordTy arm, so a record-returning opening prints nothing whatever its fields are (measured). FIRED: removing the f32 widen makes the approximate field print 0.0 instead of 2.5 and leaves the three f64 fields untouched",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ops\\real-approx-modes.codex" "the two combinations the type could not spell before the Real collapse: f32 SATURATING and f32 trapping. Precision and safety are independent, and the emitter's finite-range test uses four constants that differ by width (shl 1/shr 53 against 2047 for a double, shl 33/shr 56 against 255 for a single). Run f32 through the f64 constants and the exponent read is nonsense, the guard never fires, and saturating silently stops saturating. FIRED: forcing the f64 constant moves both overflow lines from 2139095039 (largest finite single) to 2139095040 (infinity) and moves nothing else. Both modes already shipped once ignoring infinity entirely because every operand in their tests was finite",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\ops\\real-negate.codex" "unary minus on a Real: the compiler does no float math, so the fixed point cannot see this. -(f x) where f returns Real was typed Integer, which broke foreword math Matrix4 and with it the whole 3D stack (engine quire, globe, spark). Lives in ops\\, the operator-correctness axis",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- Proof system (normalizer soundness) ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\normalize-eq.codex" "Stage 3 defeq normalizer: delta/iota reduce flip On -> Off, id-bit On -> On (proofs check by Refl)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\induction-parse.codex" "Stage 4b/5: induction on Nat CHECKS add n Zero === n (Zero->Refl, Succ->cong ih), erased CDX4020",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\induction-list.codex" "Stage 5: binary-ctor induction CHECKS append xs MyNil === xs (MyCons->cong ih, ?f := MyCons h via N-ary peel)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\induction-assoc.codex" "Stage 5b: multi-var induction via nested for-all -- append-assoc (induct on named `as`, bs/cs opaque)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\reverse-reverse.codex" "Stage 5b FLAGSHIP: reverse (reverse xs) === xs via append-nil/append-assoc/reverse-append (applicable lemmas + app-cong + capture-avoiding normalizer)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\induction-param.codex" "Stage 5c: induction over a PARAMETRIC type Lst a (checker resolves applied ConstructedTy to its SumTy)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\kleene-tribool.codex" "three-valued logic: tnot (tnot t) === t and tor t TTrue === TTrue over three NULLARY constructors, so every arm is Refl with no IH -- the induction path with no recursive field",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- Error rejection (diagnostic path) ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\normalize-false.codex" "Stage 3 soundness tripwire: flip On === On is FALSE (flip On reduces to Off), must reject CDX2001",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\induction-unsound.codex" "Stage 4b/5 soundness tripwire: Succ case proved by Refl (not cong ih) is FALSE, must reject CDX2001",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\induction-list-unsound.codex" "Stage 5 tripwire: N-ary peel injectivity -- MyCons case by Refl is FALSE, must reject CDX2001",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\reverse-reverse-unsound.codex" "Stage 5b tripwire: reverse-reverse MyCons step by cong ih alone (no reverse-append lemma) must reject CDX2001",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\kleene-excluded-middle.codex" "excluded middle over Kleene logic: tor t (tnot t) === TTrue holds at TFalse and TTrue and is FALSE at TUnknown, so TWO of three arms prove and one cannot. Rejects CDX2001 'Con:TTrue vs Con:TUnknown'. A partial refusal, which is what makes it a tripwire for the per-constructor subgoal rather than for the claim as a whole",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\type-mismatch.codex" "type error detection",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\unknown-name.codex" "undefined name detection",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\non-exhaustive-match.codex" "exhaustiveness checker",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\keyword-as-pattern-var.codex" "keyword rejection",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\linear-errors.codex" "linear type violations",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\record-field-silence.codex" "a record literal names every field, and no other: CDX2006 / CDX2005",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\effect-op-unhandled.codex" "a nullary effect op with no handler read zero and said nothing: CDX2034",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\errors\\scope-let-arm-escape.codex" "the adversarial half of 2.22: a read of a name bound only inside an if-arm's let must be rejected AT THE READ, by the RESOLVER (CDX3002). It answered CDX2040 from the emitter (\"unresolved call\" to a name nobody wrote) while both the resolver and the type env aliased their caller's scope, then CDX2002 from the checker once the type env was fixed. The program is rejected either way, so only the CODE says whether the scope discipline is intact",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- Regressions ---",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\console-readline-cite.codex" "citing Console must not disable read-line (the handler slot outranked the builtin)",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\scope-let-arm-global.codex" "the type environment has lexical scope: an if-arm's `let inner : Integer` must not still be bound after the arm, where it shadowed the global `inner : Text` and made the CHECKER reject a valid program with CDX2001 -- one the emitter compiled correctly. The fixed point cannot see this: the compiler self-compiles either way, because the leak only ever ADDED bindings and the compiler's own source never reads one out of scope",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\match-arms-per-line.codex" "a `when` keeps every `is` arm however they are packed across lines. The parser pinned `ln` to the line the match STARTED on, so the second arm of the second line matched neither the line nor the column test and SILENTLY ENDED THE MATCH -- dropping every later line including the `is otherwise`, with no diagnostic. Deliberately an Integer match: exhaustiveness was the only thing that ever caught this and it cannot fire on an open type, which is why the one site anybody found was a closed variant and the rest went unnoticed",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\scope-handler-clause.codex" "a handler clause's `resume` binder does not escape the clause body. The quietest of the scope leaks: it crashed nothing and printed a plausible wrong answer -- the read found the clause's recycled slot, which happened to hold the previously-built Text, so `after: GLOBAL` printed as `after: counter: 42`. `tick` must STILL be bound after its clause (the handled expression reads the handler slot through the op-name, added after the body on purpose), so this also pins the restore ORDERING: get it wrong and handler-smoke's multi-op and nested cases go with it",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\scope-try-region.codex" "a `trying` body's bindings do not escape into `falling back to`, `on failure`, or past the `end`. This one MISCOMPILED rather than rejecting, because the checker was already right and the resolver and emitter were not: the fallback's `label` typed as the global Text and loaded the body's Integer slot, so a wild pointer reached text concatenation. The fixed point cannot see this either -- `trying` appears in no compiler source, so the self-compile never emits a try at all and this test is the only thing between the try regions and silence",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\cite-override-quire.codex" "a cite naming its QUIRE overrides a contested name. find-slug-for-cite-name keyed on <Quire>--<Chapter> while the concat prefixes each header with its DIRECTORY, and a quire is not a directory -- all of codex/compiler is the Codex quire while sitting in Core, Emit, Types, Syntax -- so the key matched nothing for 21 of the compiler's own 73 cites and the lookup answered \"\". The consequence was not the silently-wrong definition predicted: with the cited name CONTESTED both definitions are mangled, the citing chapter gets no rename entry, and the mention resolves to nothing, so this file did not compile at all (CDX3002, no binary). It went unnoticed because every cite written that way in the tree happens to name an UNCONTESTED definition, and the fixed point cannot see it for the same reason -- the compiler self-compiles either way. Ten bare names are genuinely ambiguous in real source (Console in core and kernel, Opening in compiler and test, Markdown in encode and ui), so the bare-name fallback REFUSES rather than guessing: first-hit matching would mangle to whichever chapter the concat emitted first, which is a wrong answer that compiles",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\field-cache-text-lit.codex" "a field read twice in one call gives the same answer both times, even with a text literal between the reads. `emit-text-lit` writes RAX with a hardcoded mov-ri64 before alloc-temp runs, and alloc-temp only evicts the register it hands out -- so the field cache went on claiming `b.items` was live in RAX after the literal had overwritten it, and `list-length [7, 8, 9]` returned 9: the character count of \"read-text\". A wrong number, no crash, no diagnostic. THE FIXED POINT CANNOT SEE THIS, and green self-compiles are exactly what it produced for months: the compiler's own instance of the shape (`find-effect-op-addr (st.effect-op-addrs) \"read-text\" 0 (list-length (st.effect-op-addrs))`) walked off the end of a two-element list and found no match, which is the answer it wanted anyway. It only ever surfaced as a crash when a program's heap layout put a non-canonical pointer after the list. The literal must stay LONGER than the list or the walk stays in bounds and this passes while broken",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\desk-root-guard.codex" "the desk's root reclaim must not free a live pane's state. The guard asks the mark stack, a mark records where a pane's state STARTED, and the Browser is the one pane that rebuilds its state elsewhere on re-entry, so the guard tested an address the state no longer occupied and freed it. Shipped at main 20497 and it HALTS the guest (invalid opcode) on the second pill restore. No frozen-clock capture could see it and none ever will: `desk.ps1 -Rtc` pins the HPET, so `dk-dclick` reads an elapsed of zero and a second click on one pill is a double-click, which minimises rather than restoring. `live-at-e` is the row `desk-marks-remark` produces and the only one a sabotage of the mark test moves; `settled` is the WORKS-58 reclaim that must keep firing, and guarding on the frontier instead of the mark makes it answer no and costs 2,394,032 bytes a cycle",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\trust-vouch-depth.codex" "the vouch-walk memo is keyed on the agent AND THE DEPTH. An agent's score is not a property of the agent: the walk is capped at depth 5, so the same agent scores 8000 arriving at depth 1 and 0 arriving at depth 5, and both are right. The deep arrival is walked FIRST here, so a memo keyed on the bare agent name caches 0 and the shallow arrival reads it back -- x scores 0 instead of 6400. Measured: with the key cut to the bare agent, EVERY other trust test still passes, trust-lattice-test included, and only this one fails. A wrong trust score admits or refuses a quotation with no diagnostic anywhere",
    bvt-head "",
    bvt-head "--- The repository protocol --- these carry a .disk sidecar",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-source-fact.codex" "Codex stores its own SOURCE: a real chapter, pipes and all, written to a block device as a content-addressed Ed25519-signed fact, booted back, and admitted by the same import gate the quotation gate uses. A forged body is ImportCorrupt",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\disk-facts-multi-load.codex" "a fact bigger than one sector must not truncate the store, and one corrupt fact must not take every fact behind it",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-checkout.codex" "A CHECKOUT: 3 facts, 2 works. The checkout takes the REVISED edition of a path and leaves the superseded one behind (a checkout is a tree, not a log), comes back byte-identical, and the superseded edition is still in the store forever, addressable by its hash",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-tombstone.codex" "REMOVAL: a path is stored, retired with a tombstone, and stored again; the checked-out tree follows the last word for the path each time (store->tomb->restore), while every edition stays in wi-works addressable by its hash",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-index-snapshot.codex" "PERSIST THE INDEX: the whole materialized WorkIndex is snapshotted as a kind-40 fact, then a def is added after it; a fast rebuild (load snapshot + replay only the tail) checks out identically to a full log replay, the snapshot alone checks out the tree as of its moment, and a superseded edition is still addressable by hash -- the history survives the snapshot, not just the tree",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-tombstone-signed.codex" "AUTHENTICATED REMOVAL: a signed kind-39 tombstone the verified index checks before honoring. The owner's signed tombstone retires a.codex; a forger the manifest does not hold cannot retire b.codex (the verified index refuses it, b stays); the trusting index still drops both by path. An unsigned removal was a hole any sector-writer could use",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\repo-tombstone-replay.codex" "REPLAY DEFEATED: every assertion is validly signed by the owner -- the attack is copying an OLD signature forward to override a newer one. The verified index resolves each path by the signed timestamp, so a replayed t2 tombstone cannot retire a file re-added at t3, a replayed t1 definition cannot resurrect a file retired at t2, and a genuinely newer t9 tombstone still retires",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\fact-sync-test.codex" "REPLICATION: two content-addressed stores that overlap but differ reconcile to the union with no conflict resolution -- the shared fact is not duplicated, each side asks for exactly the fact it lacks, and merging in either direction lands on the same store",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\fact-sync-wire-test.codex" "THE WIRE VERB: the reconciliation carried as AgentMessages over TrustTransport. A offers its hashes, the offer is encoded to a tagged frame body and decoded back exactly as it would cross TCP, B answers with the one fact A lacked, that reply crosses the same wire, and A absorbs it to the union",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\checkout-emit.codex" "stage one of build/test-compile-from-store.ps1: stores a REAL PROGRAM, revises it, checks the tree back out and prints it. Its .expected IS the checked-out source, so it pins the checkout BYTE FOR BYTE. The first edition is wrong on purpose",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\colophon-dogfood.codex" "THE DOGFOOD: a two-chapter quire goes into the store, one chapter is edited and stored again, and the test prints an honest account -- what works (bytes, hashes, signatures, the gate, both editions retained forever) and what does not (ask for a chapter by name and the store hands back the last file written, whichever it was). A dogfood test that only prints its successes is a colophon",
    bvt-entry "codex\\test\\apps\\disk-facts-compact.codex" "compaction kept ONE FACT PER KIND -- it would have destroyed every source definition but one, and every secret entry, FileShare manifest and revocation record but one. A compactor that cannot prove two facts are the same must keep both"
  ]

  s02 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$BvtTests = @(", ScSequence bvt-test-list, ScRaw ")"]

Section: S03 -- Output Directories

  s03 : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "OutRoot" (SeLit "test-output"), ScAssign "ResultsDir" (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutRoot '_results'"), ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $OutRoot | Out-Null", ScIf (SeDirExists (SeVar "ResultsDir")) [ScRaw "Remove-Item -Recurse -Force $ResultsDir"] [], ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $ResultsDir | Out-Null", ScBlank, ScAssign "TestLog" (SeRaw "Join-Path $OutRoot 'bvt.log'"), ScSetContent (SeVar "TestLog") (SeLit ""), ScRaw "$env:CODEX_SWEEP_LOG = (Resolve-Path $TestLog).Path"]

Section: S04 -- Kernel Setup

  s04 : List ShellCmd =
    let copy-cdx = [ScAssign "stage0" (SeRaw "Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'build-output\\bare-metal\\Codex.cdx'"), ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path (Split-Path $stage0) | Out-Null", ScCopy (SeVar "CodexCdx") (SeVar "stage0")]
    in let no-kernel = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"ERROR: No kernel at $stage0 -- run build/build.ps1 first.\"") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in let no-vm = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"ERROR: codex-vm.exe not found at $vmExe\"") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScIf (SeVar "CodexCdx") copy-cdx [], ScBlank, ScAssign "stage0" (SeRaw "Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'build-output\\bare-metal\\Codex.cdx'"), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "stage0"))) no-kernel [], ScBlank, ScRaw "# The label travels with the list. A cited-test run that printed \"BVT\" would be", ScRaw "# read as the BVT having passed, which is a different and much stronger claim.", ScRaw "$BvtLabel = 'BVT'", ScRaw "if ($SubjectsFile) {", ScRaw "    if (-not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $SubjectsFile)) {", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"ERROR: -SubjectsFile $SubjectsFile does not exist\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "        exit 1", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $BvtTests = @(Get-Content $SubjectsFile | ForEach-Object { $_.Trim() } | Where-Object { $_ })", ScRaw "    $BvtLabel = 'CITED-RUN'", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScRaw "# The battery drops these BEFORE it compiles anything, so a runner pointed at", ScRaw "# arbitrary chapters must drop them too. The BVT's own list was chosen to avoid", ScRaw "# them, so this was never needed until the gate's cited-test phase started", ScRaw "# handing this runner whatever a CL implicated: 80 device/SMP/gpu/shell chapters", ScRaw "# went red in one arc for want of it. Widening the SUBJECTS without widening the", ScRaw "# RUNNER is L-SIDECAR, and the corpus carries 31 .skip, 4 .slow and 15 .fatal.", ScRaw "$bvtSkipped = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$BvtTests = @($BvtTests | Where-Object {", ScRaw "    $b = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($_)", ScRaw "    foreach ($m in @('skip', 'slow', 'fatal')) {", ScRaw "        if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf ($_ -replace '\\.codex$', \".$m\")) {", ScRaw "            $why = (Get-Content -TotalCount 1 ($_ -replace '\\.codex$', \".$m\") -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)", ScRaw "            $bvtSkipped.Add(\"$b ($m) $why\")", ScRaw "            return $false", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $true", ScRaw "})", ScRaw "foreach ($sk in $bvtSkipped) { Write-Host \"  SKIP  $sk\" -ForegroundColor DarkGray }", ScBlank, ScAssign "vmExe" (SeRaw "Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'tools\\codex-vm.exe'"), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "vmExe"))) no-vm []]

Section: S05 -- Missing Files Check

  s05 : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "missing" (SeRaw "@()"), ScForEach "t" (SeVar "BvtTests") [ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "t"))) [ScRaw "$missing += $t"] []], ScIf (SeRaw "$missing.Count -gt 0") [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"ERROR: Missing $BvtLabel test files:\"") ClBrightRed True, ScForEach "m" (SeVar "missing") [ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  $m\"")], ScExit (SeInt 1)] []]

Section: S06 -- Timer and Header

  s06 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$sw = [System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch]::StartNew()", ScEcho (SeRaw "\"${BvtLabel}: $($BvtTests.Count) tests, $Jobs parallel slots\""), ScEcho (SeLit "")]

Section: S07 -- Phase 1 Compile

  s07 : List ShellCmd = [ScEcho (SeLit "--- Phase 1: compile ---"), ScAssign "compileScript" (SeRaw "Join-Path (Resolve-Path .).Path 'build\\compile.ps1'"), ScRaw "$compileFails = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$compilePass = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()"]

Section: S08 -- Parallel Compile Loop

  s08 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$BvtTests | ForEach-Object -ThrottleLimit $Jobs -Parallel {", ScRaw "    $t = $_", ScRaw "    $base = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($t)", ScRaw "    $outDir = Join-Path $using:OutRoot $base", ScRaw "    $cdxOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.cdx\"", ScRaw "    $logOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.log\"", ScRaw "    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $outDir | Out-Null", ScRaw "    $failFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.failing'", ScRaw "    $expectFail = Test-Path $failFile", ScRaw "    # The .flags sidecar rides along, exactly as test.ps1 does it. Without it a", ScRaw "    # subject that needs decks=200 (foreword-all-compile) fails to compile here", ScRaw "    # while compiling fine everywhere else, and the runner is measuring its own", ScRaw "    # invocation rather than the test (L-SIDECAR).", ScRaw "    $flagsFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.flags'", ScRaw "    $rawFlags = if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $flagsFile) { (Get-Content -TotalCount 1 $flagsFile).Trim() } else { '' }", ScRaw "    $cArgs = @('-NoProfile', '-File', $using:compileScript, '-Src', $t, '-Out', $cdxOut, '-Log', $logOut)", ScRaw "    if ($rawFlags) { $cArgs += @('-RawFlags', $rawFlags) }", ScRaw "    $r = & pwsh @cArgs 2>&1", ScRaw "    $ok = $LASTEXITCODE -eq 0", ScRaw "    if ($expectFail) {", ScRaw "        if ($ok) {", ScRaw "            ($using:compileFails).Add(\"$base (expected compile FAIL but got PASS)\")", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (expected compile failure)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "        } else {", ScRaw "            $codes = @(Get-Content $failFile -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | ForEach-Object { $_.Trim() } | Where-Object { $_ })", ScRaw "            $logText = if (Test-Path $logOut) { Get-Content $logOut -Raw -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue } else { '' }", ScRaw "            $allFound = $true", ScRaw "            # test.ps1 594-602's adjudication, and it has to stay identical to it. A", ScRaw "            # ^\\d+$ filter here dropped every CDX-prefixed sidecar -- 45 of the 176,", ScRaw "            # five of them BVT's own CDX2001 proof tripwires (normalize-false,", ScRaw "            # induction-unsound, induction-list-unsound, reverse-reverse-unsound,", ScRaw "            # kleene-excluded-middle) -- leaving those checked against NO codes, so any", ScRaw "            # compile failure passed them: a tripwire that cannot fail (L-FALSIF). A", ScRaw "            # bare CDX<n> search is the other half, and it cannot match the lexer's", ScRaw "            # unprefixed codes (\"error 6:\"), which reads as a wrong-code failure.", ScRaw "            foreach ($code in $codes) {", ScRaw "                if ($code -match '^(?<c>(CDX)?\\d+)@(?<l>\\d+):(?<col>\\d+)$') {", ScRaw "                    $cc = $matches['c'] -replace '^CDX', ''", ScRaw "                    if ($logText -notmatch \"\\b$($matches['l']):$($matches['col']):\\s*error (CDX)?0*$cc\\b\") { $allFound = $false }", ScRaw "                } elseif ($logText -notmatch \"error (CDX)?0*$code\\b\") { $allFound = $false }", ScRaw "            }", ScRaw "            if ($allFound) {", ScRaw "                ($using:compilePass).Add($base)", ScRaw "                Write-Host \"  PASS  $base (expected error)\" -ForegroundColor Green", ScRaw "            } else {", ScRaw "                ($using:compileFails).Add(\"$base (missing expected CDX codes: $($codes -join ','))\")", ScRaw "                Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (wrong error codes)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "            }", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    } else {", ScRaw "        if ($ok) {", ScRaw "            ($using:compilePass).Add($base)", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"  PASS  $base\" -ForegroundColor Green", ScRaw "        } else {", ScRaw "            ($using:compileFails).Add(\"$base (compile failed)\")", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (compile)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "}"]

Section: S09 -- Phase 2 Run Header

  s09 : List ShellCmd = [ScEcho (SeLit ""), ScEcho (SeLit "--- Phase 2: run ---"), ScRaw "$runFails = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$runPass = [System.Collections.Concurrent.ConcurrentBag[string]]::new()", ScAssign "runSkip" (SeInt 0), ScBlank, ScRaw "$runnableTests = $BvtTests | Where-Object { $exp = $_ -replace '\\.codex$', '.expected'; Test-Path $exp }"]

Section: S10 -- Parallel Run Loop

  s10 : List ShellCmd = [ScComment "One codex-vm -run-list supervisor per job slot, a fresh codex-vm child per", ScComment "test, so the cold boot a single run proves is unchanged (OperatorsManual", ScComment "\"Batch mode: -run-list\"). Measured 2026-08-22: the pwsh child running", ScComment "test-run.ps1 was 501 of the 575 ms a test cost here. The sidecar copy", ScComment "test-run.ps1 did stays with the caller: a depot .disk is read-only after", ScComment "sync and codex-vm flushes writes durably, so each gets a writable temp.", ScRaw "$runList = @($runnableTests)", ScRaw "$runDir = Join-Path $OutRoot '_bvt-runs'", ScRaw "if (Test-Path $runDir) { Remove-Item -Recurse -Force $runDir }", ScRaw "New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $runDir | Out-Null", ScRaw "$slotLines = @{}", ScRaw "for ($s = 0; $s -lt $Jobs; $s++) { $slotLines[$s] = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new() }", ScRaw "$tempDisks = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()", ScRaw "$rawOf = @{}", ScRaw "$lineKey = @{}", ScRaw "for ($i = 0; $i -lt $runList.Count; $i++) {", ScRaw "    $t = $runList[$i]", ScRaw "    $base = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($t)", ScRaw "    $outDir = Join-Path $OutRoot $base", ScRaw "    $cdxOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.cdx\"", ScRaw "    if (-not (Test-Path $cdxOut)) { continue }", ScRaw "    $raw = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.raw\"", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path $raw) { Remove-Item -Force $raw }", ScRaw "    $rawOf[$base] = $raw", ScRaw "    $tokens = @('-kernel', $cdxOut, '-output', $raw, '-mem', '3072', '-headless')", ScRaw "    # Every machine sidecar test-run.ps1 passes, mapped to the same codex-vm", ScRaw "    # flags in the same order. A subject whose SUBJECT IS THE MACHINE (a bus", ScRaw "    # topology, an absent device, a second drive, more than one core) answers", ScRaw "    # nothing without these, and the failure reads as a miscompile: the 80 reds", ScRaw "    # of blu's arc were smp-* booting single-core, usb-kbd-*/pci-bridge-*/e1000-*", ScRaw "    # with no topology, and shell-repl/diagnostic-boot with no stdin.", ScRaw "    $stdinFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.stdin'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $stdinFile) {", ScRaw "        $inWork = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()", ScRaw "        $tempDisks.Add($inWork)", ScRaw "        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($inWork, [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($stdinFile))", ScRaw "        $tokens += @('-input', $inWork)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    # Read in place: codex-vm only reads it, so the read-only attribute a depot", ScRaw "    # sidecar carries after sync is no obstacle.", ScRaw "    $keysFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.keys'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $keysFile) { $tokens += @('-keys-file', $keysFile) }", ScRaw "    $diskFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.disk'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $diskFile) {", ScRaw "        $diskWork = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()", ScRaw "        $tempDisks.Add($diskWork)", ScRaw "        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($diskWork, [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($diskFile))", ScRaw "        $tokens += @('-disk', $diskWork)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    # .disk-src names ANOTHER test whose freshly compiled CDX becomes this", ScRaw "    # test's disk, which is the point: a test pinning what the CURRENT compiler", ScRaw "    # emits cannot use a frozen image.", ScRaw "    $diskSrcFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.disk-src'", ScRaw "    if ((Test-Path -PathType Leaf $diskSrcFile) -and -not (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $diskFile)) {", ScRaw "        $srcName = (Get-Content -TotalCount 1 $diskSrcFile).Trim()", ScRaw "        $srcCdx = Join-Path (Join-Path $OutRoot $srcName) \"$srcName.cdx\"", ScRaw "        if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $srcCdx) {", ScRaw "            $dsWork = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()", ScRaw "            $tempDisks.Add($dsWork)", ScRaw "            [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($dsWork, [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($srcCdx))", ScRaw "            $tokens += @('-disk', $dsWork)", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    # The primary channel's slave, and it matters more than the master here: the", ScRaw "    # case it exists for is one drive writing to another.", ScRaw "    $disk2File = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.disk2'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $disk2File) {", ScRaw "        $disk2Work = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()", ScRaw "        $tempDisks.Add($disk2Work)", ScRaw "        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($disk2Work, [System.IO.File]::ReadAllBytes($disk2File))", ScRaw "        $tokens += @('-disk2', $disk2Work)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $smpFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.smp'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $smpFile) {", ScRaw "        $smpN = 0", ScRaw "        if ([int]::TryParse((Get-Content -TotalCount 1 $smpFile).Trim(), [ref]$smpN) -and $smpN -gt 1) {", ScRaw "            $tokens += @('-smp', \"$smpN\")", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    # Whitespace-separated flags, '#' comments and blank lines ignored.", ScRaw "    $vmArgsFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.vmargs'", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $vmArgsFile) {", ScRaw "        foreach ($vline in (Get-Content $vmArgsFile)) {", ScRaw "            $vline = $vline.Trim()", ScRaw "            if (-not $vline -or $vline.StartsWith('#')) { continue }", ScRaw "            $tokens += ($vline -split '\\s+')", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $s = $i % $Jobs", ScRaw "    # Every token double-quoted: that is what -run-list's splitter takes.", ScRaw "    $slotLines[$s].Add((($tokens | ForEach-Object { '\"' + $_ + '\"' }) -join ' '))", ScRaw "    $lineKey[$base] = \"$s/$($slotLines[$s].Count)\"", ScRaw "}", ScRaw "$supervisors = @{}", ScRaw "$slotErrs = @{}", ScRaw "for ($s = 0; $s -lt $Jobs; $s++) {", ScRaw "    if ($slotLines[$s].Count -eq 0) { continue }", ScRaw "    $lf = Join-Path $runDir \"run-$s.txt\"", ScRaw "    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllLines($lf, $slotLines[$s], [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))", ScRaw "    # The supervisor's stderr is captured on the SYSTEM temp and moved into", ScRaw "    # _bvt-runs afterwards. Measured 2026-08-22: the same eight supervisors", ScRaw "    # took 2.6 s with the redirect file on C: and 12.3 to 12.7 s with it", ScRaw "    # anywhere on D:, repo or not; a redirect is one write per stderr line", ScRaw "    # and D: pays ~7.5 ms for each. test-run.ps1 only ever escaped this", ScRaw "    # because GetTempFileName() lands on C:.", ScRaw "    $slotErrs[$s] = [System.IO.Path]::GetTempFileName()", ScRaw "    $sa = @{ FilePath = $vmExe; ArgumentList = @('-run-list', $lf); PassThru = $true; RedirectStandardError = $slotErrs[$s] }", ScRaw "    if ($IsWindows) { $sa.WindowStyle = 'Hidden' }", ScRaw "    $supervisors[$s] = Start-Process @sa", ScRaw "}", ScRaw "foreach ($s in $supervisors.Keys) { $supervisors[$s].WaitForExit() }", ScComment "One END line per list line, keyed by slot and [i/N] index, so a line the", ScComment "supervisor could not report reads as missing on its own test only.", ScRaw "$endOf = @{}", ScRaw "foreach ($s in $supervisors.Keys) {", ScRaw "    foreach ($l in @(Get-Content $slotErrs[$s] -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue)) {", ScRaw "        if ($l -match 'RUN-LIST END \\[(\\d+)/\\d+\\] .* exit=(\\S+) output=(-?\\d+) dropped=(\\d+) ms=(\\d+)') {", ScRaw "            $endOf[\"$s/$($matches[1])\"] = @{ Exit = $matches[2]; Dropped = [long]$matches[4] }", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    if (Test-Path -PathType Leaf $slotErrs[$s]) { Move-Item -Force $slotErrs[$s] (Join-Path $runDir \"run-$s.err\") }", ScRaw "}", ScRaw "foreach ($f in $tempDisks) { Remove-Item -Force $f -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }", ScBlank, ScRaw "foreach ($t in $runList) {", ScRaw "    $base = [System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($t)", ScRaw "    $outDir = Join-Path $OutRoot $base", ScRaw "    $runOut = Join-Path $outDir \"$base.out\"", ScRaw "    $expFile = $t -replace '\\.codex$', '.expected'", ScRaw "    if (-not $rawOf.ContainsKey($base)) {", ScRaw "        $runFails.Add(\"$base (no CDX to run)\")", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"  SKIP  $base (no CDX)\" -ForegroundColor Yellow", ScRaw "        continue", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $why = ''", ScRaw "    if (-not $endOf.ContainsKey($lineKey[$base])) { $why = 'no END line from the -run-list supervisor' }", ScRaw "    else {", ScRaw "        $e = $endOf[$lineKey[$base]]", ScRaw "        if ($e.Exit -eq 'TIMEOUT') { $why = 'wall budget exceeded' }", ScRaw "        elseif ($e.Exit -eq 'SPAWNFAIL') { $why = 'codex-vm could not be spawned' }", ScRaw "        elseif ($e.Dropped -gt 0) { $why = \"SHORT capture: codex-vm dropped $($e.Dropped) guest serial bytes, not codegen; re-run\" }", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    if ($why) {", ScRaw "        $runFails.Add(\"$base ($why)\")", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base ($why)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "        continue", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    $raw = $rawOf[$base]", ScRaw "    if (-not (Test-Path $raw) -or (Get-Item $raw).Length -eq 0) {", ScRaw "        $runFails.Add(\"$base (no output)\")", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (no output)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "        continue", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    # Filtered exactly as test-run.ps1 filtered it: CR and a leading SOH", ScRaw "    # stripped, HEAP:/WD:/STACK: telemetry dropped, trailing blank lines cut.", ScRaw "    $rawText = (Get-Content $raw -Raw -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) -replace \"`r\", '' -replace \"^\\x01\", ''", ScRaw "    $kept = [System.Collections.Generic.List[string]]::new()", ScRaw "    foreach ($l in ($rawText -split \"`n\")) {", ScRaw "        if ($l.StartsWith('HEAP:') -or $l.StartsWith('WD:') -or $l.StartsWith('STACK:')) { continue }", ScRaw "        [void]$kept.Add($l)", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "    while ($kept.Count -gt 0 -and $kept[$kept.Count - 1] -eq '') { $kept.RemoveAt($kept.Count - 1) }", ScRaw "    $actual = if ($kept.Count -gt 0) { ($kept -join \"`n\") + \"`n\" } else { '' }", ScRaw "    [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($runOut, $actual, [System.Text.UTF8Encoding]::new($false))", ScRaw "    $expected = (Get-Content $expFile -Raw -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) -replace \"`r\", ''", ScRaw "    $actual = $actual.TrimEnd(\"`n\")", ScRaw "    $expected = $expected.TrimEnd(\"`n\")", ScRaw "    if ($actual -eq $expected) {", ScRaw "        $runPass.Add($base)", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"  PASS  $base\" -ForegroundColor Green", ScRaw "    } else {", ScRaw "        # LENGTH BEFORE CONTENT (L-SHORT). The two 80-character excerpts below", ScRaw "        # are identical for a truncated capture and for a miscompile, so on their", ScRaw "        # own they invite every red here to be read as codegen. A strict PREFIX", ScRaw "        # is the signature of a capture cut off mid-stream and a miscompile has", ScRaw "        # no reason to produce one; a bare length difference proves nothing,", ScRaw "        # since ordinary wrong output differs in length too. Report the two as", ScRaw "        # different claims and say the lengths either way.", ScRaw "        $lim = [Math]::Min($expected.Length, $actual.Length)", ScRaw "        $off = 0", ScRaw "        while ($off -lt $lim -and $expected[$off] -eq $actual[$off]) { $off++ }", ScRaw "        if ($actual.Length -lt $expected.Length -and $off -eq $actual.Length) {", ScRaw "            $runFails.Add(\"$base (output TRUNCATED: $($actual.Length) of $($expected.Length) chars, a strict prefix -- SHORT capture, not codegen; re-run)\")", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (output TRUNCATED)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"    actual $($actual.Length) chars is a strict PREFIX of the expected $($expected.Length): the capture is SHORT, not wrong. Re-run before reading this as codegen (L-SHORT)\" -ForegroundColor DarkGray", ScRaw "        } else {", ScRaw "            $runFails.Add(\"$base (output mismatch: $($actual.Length) chars vs expected $($expected.Length), diverges at offset $off)\")", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"  FAIL  $base (output mismatch)\" -ForegroundColor Red", ScRaw "            Write-Host \"    actual $($actual.Length) chars, expected $($expected.Length), diverges at offset $off -- not a prefix, so this is a content difference (L-SHORT)\" -ForegroundColor DarkGray", ScRaw "        }", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"    expected: $($expected.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(80, $expected.Length)))\" -ForegroundColor DarkGray", ScRaw "        Write-Host \"    actual:   $($actual.Substring(0, [Math]::Min(80, $actual.Length)))\" -ForegroundColor DarkGray", ScRaw "    }", ScRaw "}"]

Section: S11 -- Results Summary

  s11 : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "$sw.Stop()", ScRaw "$totalPass = $compilePass.Count + $runPass.Count", ScRaw "$totalFail = $compileFails.Count + $runFails.Count", ScEcho (SeLit ""), ScEcho (SeLit "--- BVT Results ---"), ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Compile: $($compilePass.Count) pass, $($compileFails.Count) fail\""), ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Runtime: $($runPass.Count) pass, $($runFails.Count) fail\""), ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Total:   $totalPass pass, $totalFail fail\""), ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Time:    $([math]::Round($sw.Elapsed.TotalSeconds, 1))s\"")]

Section: S12 -- Failure Report and Exit

  s12 : List ShellCmd = [ScIf (SeRaw "$totalFail -gt 0") [ScEcho (SeLit ""), ScEchoStyled (SeLit "FAILURES:") ClBrightRed True, ScForEach "f" (SeVar "compileFails") [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"  $f\"") ClBrightRed True], ScForEach "f" (SeVar "runFails") [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"  $f\"") ClBrightRed True], ScExit (SeInt 1)] [], ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit ""), ScEchoStyled (SeLit "BVT PASSED") ClBrightGreen True, ScExit (SeInt 0)]

Section: Assembly

  bvt-body : List ShellCmd = [ScSequence s01, ScBlank, ScSequence s02, ScBlank, ScSequence s03, ScBlank, ScSequence s04, ScBlank, ScSequence s05, ScBlank, ScSequence s06, ScBlank, ScSequence s07, ScBlank, ScSequence s08, ScBlank, ScSequence s09, ScBlank, ScSequence s10, ScBlank, ScSequence s11, ScBlank, ScSequence s12]

  bvt-script : ShellScript = sh-script "bvt" "Build Verification Test - minimal confidence gate" bvt-params bvt-body

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell bvt-script)
  end

Page 1
